<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H12089</pnldref><english><title>Member of a jury at an inquest research the case during the inquest period</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>research</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>inquest</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>jury</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>Coroners and Justice Act 2009</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>criminal justice and courts act 2015</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>schedule 13</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..), being a member of a jury at an inquest, namely **(..IDENTIFY THE INQUEST DETAILS..), researched the case during the inquest period, in that you **(..SPECIFY THE RESEARCH UNDERTAKEN..)</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to paragraph 5A(1) and (8) of Schedule 6 to the Coroners and Justice Act 2009.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt;member of a jury at an inquest&lt;br /&gt;researched the case during the inquest period</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>(i) A person researches a case if (and only if) the person intentionally seeks information and, when doing so, knows or ought reasonably to know that the information is or may be relevant to the inquest.&lt;br /&gt;(ii) Definitions and exceptions relating the offence can be found in paragraph 5A of Schedule 6</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>IND</code><description>INDICTABLE</description></modeoftrial><consents><consent><code>A</code><description>Attorney General</description></consent></consents><timelimitforprosecutions>None</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>Indictment: Two years imprisonment and / or a fine&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Time limit on Prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt;None</penalty><geographicregion><code>EWNI</code><description>England, Wales and Northern Ireland</description></geographicregion></other><codes><cjsoffencecode>CJ09023</cjsoffencecode><recordableonpncindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></recordableonpncindicator><notifiabletoho><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></notifiabletoho><hoclassification>079/10</hoclassification><mopireviewgroup><code>C</code><description>Group 3</descripti